{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "10667_ikeru",
  "headword": "{生|い}ける",
  "reading": "いける",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to arrange (flowers)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to arrange flowers, to do ikebana",
      "explanation": "To arrange cut flowers or branches in a vase or container, especially in the traditional Japanese art of flower arrangement (生け花)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10667_ikeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{花|はな}を{生|い}ける。",
      "english": "To arrange flowers.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10667_ikeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{母|はは}は{毎週|まいしゅう}、{玄関|げんかん}に{花|はな}を{生|い}けている。",
      "english": "My mother arranges flowers in the entryway every week.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10667_ikeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{庭|にわ}で{摘|つ}んだ{花|はな}を{和室|わしつ}の{花瓶|かびん}に{生|い}けた。",
      "english": "I arranged flowers I picked from the garden in the vase in the Japanese-style room.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). Takes を for the flowers being arranged.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {生|い}け{花|ばな} / {生|い}け{花|はな}: ikebana, the art of flower arrangement\n- {花瓶|かびん}: flower vase\n\nWRITING:\nUsually written as {生|い}ける. Also sometimes written as {活|い}ける with the same meaning.\n\nNOTE: This is a different word from the colloquial いける (to be doable, to be okay).",
